1004
"Bit sequnce normal start/stop from remote:

Before start:
CW bit0=0 On/OFF1
CW,bit3=0 Operation enable
SW bit0=1 ready on (normal always true)
SW bit1=0 ready run (controlled by CW bit0 OFF1)
SW bit2=0 ready ref, if true converter running.

Start:
CW bit0=1 On/OFF1
CW bit3=1 Operation enable
SW bit0=1 ready on
SW bit1=1 ready run 
SW bit2=1 ready ref

Stop:
CW bit0=1 On/OFF1
CW bit3=0 Operation enable
SW bit0=1 ready on 
SW bit1=1 ready run
SW bit2=0 ready ref
 
Stop ends (zero speed):
CW bit0=0 On/OFF1
CW bit3=0 Operation enable
SW bit0=1 ready on 
SW bit1=0 ready run
SW bit2=0 ready ref

If SW bit0 is forced to false (tripped converter etc), CW bit0 must go/be false
to enable SW bit0 to be true, i.e. CW bit0 is edge sensitive in some cases."
